🔌 The story of MCP

MCP was created by Anthropic, the AI company behind Claude.

6
🇺🇸 Who created it?

Anthropic — an American AI company based in San Francisco, California, USA.

MCP was introduced publicly by Anthropic in November 2024.

The idea was simple:

“AI models need an easy, standard way to connect to external tools and information.”

Before MCP, developers often had to build different custom integrations for different AI applications and tools.

🧩 The problem before MCP

Imagine you have:

AI
 ↓
Database

Then you want:

AI → GitHub
AI → Google Drive
AI → Database
AI → Slack
AI → Weather API

Developers could create separate connections for each one.

That becomes messy.

========

💡 Then MCP came

Anthropic proposed a standard protocol for connecting AI applications to external tools and data.

Think about USB.

Before USB, different devices could have different connectors.

USB gave computers a common connection standard.

MCP is similar in concept:

MCP = a common standard for AI ↔ tools/data communication.

==========

🚗 Your EV project example

Suppose your EV forecasting agent needs:

EV charging data
Weather information
Database records
Forecast results

Without MCP:

AI Agent
 ├── Custom EV API code
 ├── Custom Weather API code
 ├── Custom Database code
 └── Custom File code

With MCP:

             AI Agent
                ↓
               MCP
                ↓
       ┌────────┼────────┐
       ↓        ↓        ↓
      EV API  Weather  Database

The important point is that MCP is a protocol, not another AI model.

